 "9963": {
  "en": [
   "They seek love for the sake of happiness; love is not found,",
   "and happiness alone slips away.",
   "Such is the trickery of illusion.",
   "They forget whom they leave, whom they desire.",
   "So the night passes in weeping, so the heart burns,",
   "so the sulks and wounded pride,",
   "so all this crying alas, alas.",
   "Only forgetting joy and sorrow in love does one find joy.",
   "Come, friend; the night is gone, the dream is ended;",
   "why keep on in vain, tell me.",
   "The moon has carried sleep's enchantment down to the western hill.",
   "Come, friend.",
   "The tale of love, the song — it has come to an end.",
   "Now some laugh, and some sit shedding tears."
